diff --git a/changelog.d/pr505.feature.rst b/changelog.d/pr505.feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b37fd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/pr505.feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+All ``pysemver`` subcommands now accept an optional leading ``v`` or ``V``
+on version arguments (for example a git tag like ``v1.4.2``). The output
+is printed without the prefix.
diff --git a/changelog.d/pr506.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/pr506.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..30d0327
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/pr506.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Passing a :class:`dict` to :meth:`Version.compare` is deprecated and now emits a :class:`DeprecationWarning`. Use ``Version(**mapping)`` instead. Strings, tuples, lists and :class:`Version` instances are still accepted.
diff --git a/changelog.d/pr507.deprecation.rst b/changelog.d/pr507.deprecation.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9e803d7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/pr507.deprecation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+:meth:`Version.next_version` now names its prerelease keyword ``token``, matching :meth:`Version.bump_prerelease` and :meth:`Version.bump_build`. The old ``prerelease_token=`` keyword is deprecated but keeps working unchanged, and does not emit a warning.
